      "message": "Ok, thanks for explaining this offline, now I see that `can_optimize()` prevents calling `copy_optimized_instructions()` etc if the range [addr; addr + JMP32_INSN_SIZE) is not within a function (and that prior `within_kprobe_blacklist()` check + your next patch ensures that if it is within a function, it is not a pKVM\u0027s function).\n\nRegarding checking `is_pkvm_text()` in `__jump_label_text_reserved()`: as we discussed offline, it seems to me that would be still hacky, as it would mean relying on some assumptions about how exactly `jump_label_text_reserved()` is used.\n\nSo perhaps this hack with returning 0 size in x86 code is still the better option short-term (until we figure out the right way to solve this)... I\u0027d just suggest to add a comment in the code to explain why we are returning 0 and why we assume it is safe to do (albeit hacky).\n\n...But I just got another idea: what if we simply give the host _read-only_ access to pKVM\u0027s text (like pKVM-ARM already does: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20250909133631.3844423-3-smostafa@google.com/)?",
